## Scope and limitations
All images are static original design candidates, not animation frames, rigged models or production-calibrated bakes. Requested 35.2643897-degree elevation / 45-degree azimuth is an approximate concept view. Mirror duelist is shallower than target. The grave spider shows seven clear tips with the fourth far leg occluded by its abdomen/rear grouping. Fine crossbow strings, bird feet, root tips and penitent limbs need actual runtime-scale testing.

Native RGBA pixels and alpha are preserved. Hidden color under transparent alpha can look like a halo in some viewers; use the supplied composited sheets. Some native frames have very narrow clear margins despite prompt instructions.

All retained assets are explicitly marked; selective repair candidates not selected were deliberately kept rather than silently claimed as rebuilt. No item/equipment assets are included in this character-only delivery.

## Padded import derivatives
30 fresh selected images also have separate import_padded/ derivatives. These only extend the canvas with transparent pixels to at least 96 pixels of visible clearance on each side. Native source and selected pack files remain unchanged. padded_import_manifest.json records integer source offset, exact native/padded canvas and visible bounds, and provisional ground-pivot coordinate shifts. Every embedded native RGBA rectangle was compared byte-for-byte after decoding. No resampling, alpha cleanup, cropping or recoloring was used.
